bibliograph (0.1.23) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bound `listShelvesWithBooks`. It hydrated every book of every shelf it
    returned, and one production shelf holds 2,573 books: a single call pinned
    the one core for 682 s while every other XRPC call, cheap ones included,
    queued behind it. The query is now a preview - at most `booksPerShelf` books
    per shelf (new parameter, 1-100, default 25) - and the full listing stays on
    `listBooksOnShelf`.
  * Cut the preview at a deadline. Shelves are fetched one indexed query at a
    time, the loop stops at 5 s, and Postgres cancels the statement at 4 s, so a
    slow shelf truncates the preview instead of holding the request open. The
    shelves and the cursor are still returned, which is the useful part.
  * Per-shelf queries also narrow to the shelf's own DID, so a Bookhive reader's
    status-matched books can no longer be filed onto every shelf with that rkey.
  * Verified against a 300-book shelf: 25 books by default, 5 with
    `booksPerShelf=5`, an out-of-range value rejected by lexicon validation, and
    a page under 100 ms.

