bibliograph (0.1.19) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Repair the legacy `bookShelving` rows instead of teaching readers a second
    shape. 2,822 mirrored rows carry `book: { ref, title }` where the lexicon
    declares `book: { uri, cid }`, and the mirror predicates
    (`value->'book'->>'uri'`) cannot see them — so `getShelvingOfBook` and
    `getShelversOfBook` answered empty for books those rows shelve. The readers
    go back to the declared shape; `scripts/normalize-legacy-shelving.ts`
    rewrites the mirrored values, taking each `cid` from the catalog row the
    record points at. Idempotent, `--dry`, `--limit`, and it reports rows whose
    edition is not in the catalog so `backfill:shelving-editions` can run first.
  * Revert the shape-tolerant reader added in 0.1.18 — with the rows repaired,
    an accessor that accepts `ref` would only hide the next divergence.
  * Drop the same tolerance from the fill job, for the same reason: it now
    resolves the declared `uri` (or the rkey fallback), and the repair script is
    what makes legacy rows visible to it.
  * The records on their authors' PDSes are untouched: this service is read-only
    and those repos are not ours. What is repaired is our copy — the mirror every
    query and hydrator reads.

